  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "It took 813 troops and B-52 bombers to trim a tree. The tree was in the Korean Demilitarized Zone.",
        "visual_query": "korean dmz border fence guard post",
        "visual_fallback": "border fence"
      },
      {
        "narration": "On the eighteenth of August, 1976, a small work party started pruning a poplar. North Korean soldiers attacked them with axes.",
        "visual_query": "tall poplar tree summer green",
        "visual_fallback": "poplar tree"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Two American officers died. Bonifas and Barrett. The tree had been blocking the sightline between a checkpoint and an observation post.",
        "visual_query": "joint security area panmunjom buildings",
        "visual_fallback": "panmunjom buildings"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Three days later the UN Command came back to finish the job. Engineers, special forces, 27 helicopters, fighters overhead, bombers behind them.",
        "visual_query": "military helicopters formation flying low",
        "visual_fallback": "military helicopters"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The tree came down in 42 minutes. Nobody fired. North Korea then accepted responsibility, which it had not done once since 1953.",
        "visual_query": "tree stump cut forest clearing",
        "visual_fallback": "tree stump"
      }
    ],
